  "id": "COMPOUND:38929 - PROTEIN:6231",
  "verbalization": "Phytuberol is implicated in the regulation of Histone-lysine N-methyltransferase, H3 lysine-9 specific 5, through a multi-step pathway involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This complex is targeted by multiple compounds, including (+)-Phylliroside, quillaic acid, and pioglitazone, all of which are known to interact with histone methyltransferases. The evidence suggests that Phytuberol may exert its effects by modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, potentially influencing the methylation of histone H3 lysine 9. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Phytuberol could interact with histone methyltransferases, possibly through the inhibition or activation of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The recurring involvement of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex as a target of multiple compounds underscores its role in the regulation of histone methylation, and the presence of multiple targets in this pathway suggests a complex, possibly redundant, regulatory network.",
